:answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562332} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2725edec-e9e4-5fb5-993b-32b7e209acd0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561687}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2725edec-e9e4-5fb5-993b-32b7e209acd0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561687} :answer-field/id #uuid "d0bee359-1a75-5e2f-8f5b-e36a4511f781" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562354}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4de28170-b86e-539e-8022-1a0054f8d5b3" :question/math-academy-id "q-253260" :question/problem "Let ${J}_{n}(\\lambda )$ denote an $n\\times n$ Jordan block with $\\lambda $ on the main diagonal. Fill in the missing entries in the matrix below.\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">$\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3{J}_{2}(\\frac{\\pi }{6}))=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-3}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"30px\">{{field-4}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "Given a function $f$ and a Jordan block ${J}_{n}(\\lambda ),$ we have\n\n$$\nf({J}_{n}(\\lambda ))=[\\begin{aligned}f(\\lambda ) & {f}^{′}(\\lambda ) & \\frac{{f}^{″}(\\lambda )}{2!} & ⋯ & \\frac{{f}^{(n-1)}(\\lambda )}{(n-1)!} \\\\ 0 & f(\\lambda ) & {f}^{′}(\\lambda ) & ⋯ & \\frac{{f}^{(n-2)}(\\lambda )}{(n-2)!} \\\\ ⋮ & ⋱ & ⋱ & ⋱ & ⋮ \\\\ 0 & ⋯ & 0 & f(\\lambda ) & {f}^{′}(\\lambda ) \\\\ 0 & ⋯ & ⋯ & 0 & f(\\lambda )\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIn this case, we have $f(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x,$ $n=2,$ and $\\lambda =\\frac{\\pi }{6}.$\n\nSince $n=2,$ we need to compute the first $2-1=1$ derivative of $f:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x \\\\ {f}^{′}(x) & =3\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f({J}_{2}(\\frac{\\pi }{6})) & =[\\begin{aligned}f(\\frac{\\pi }{6}) & {f}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{6}) \\\\ 0 & f(\\frac{\\pi }{6})\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}) & 3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}) \\\\ 0 & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186414006 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157269 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8ce12d6f-8d1c-52f3-992f-534b9d91dda9" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Value of a Function of a Jordan Block"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7f52e38a-24e3-5e4b-ac01-1a4c1fa10cf8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413971}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7f52e38a-24e3-5e4b-ac01-1a4c1fa10cf8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413971} :answer-field/id #uuid "093ddcaf-e7d3-52fa-b839-ddb952fa312d" :answer-field/key "field-5" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413983} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6955b1a9-a439-57c6-9b26-fa5bc116e904" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\ln 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413965}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6955b1a9-a439-5