er/value "\\ln 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413968} :answer-field/id #uuid "ca7af99b-f3db-551f-a410-e7335484fbb7" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413994} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c6cea381-d89c-5a7b-a546-90c344bcd752" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413979}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c6cea381-d89c-5a7b-a546-90c344bcd752" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413979} :answer-field/id #uuid "d8825eea-6236-5c45-a6bf-fa0d2e334802" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413998}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "da6ab59f-cfd7-5d6f-94dd-f3fddb0a05c8" :question/math-academy-id "q-253391" :question/problem "Let ${J}_{n}(\\lambda )$ denote an $n\\times n$ Jordan block with $\\lambda $ on the main diagonal. Fill in the missing entries in the matrix below.\n\n|  |  | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} | {{field-3}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\operatorname{ln}⁡({J}_{3}(2))=\\,\\,$ |  | $0$ | {{field-4}} | {{field-5}} |  |\n|  |  | $0$ | $0$ | {{field-6}} |  |" :question/worked-solution "Given a function $f$ and a Jordan block ${J}_{n}(\\lambda ),$ we have\n\n$$\nf({J}_{n}(\\lambda ))=\\begin{bmatrix}f(\\lambda ) & {f}^{′}(\\lambda ) & \\frac{{f}^{″}(\\lambda )}{2!} & ⋯ & \\frac{{f}^{(n-1)}(\\lambda )}{(n-1)!} \\\\ 0 & f(\\lambda ) & {f}^{′}(\\lambda ) & ⋯ & \\frac{{f}^{(n-2)}(\\lambda )}{(n-2)!} \\\\ ⋮ & ⋱ & ⋱ & ⋱ & ⋮ \\\\ 0 & ⋯ & 0 & f(\\lambda ) & {f}^{′}(\\lambda ) \\\\ 0 & ⋯ & ⋯ & 0 & f(\\lambda )\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, we have $f(x)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x,$ $n=3,$ and $\\lambda =2.$\n\nSince $n=3,$ we need to compute the first $3-1=2$ derivative of $f:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡x \\\\ {f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{1}{x} \\\\ {f}^{″}(x) & =-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f({J}_{3}(2)) & =\\begin{bmatrix}f(2) & {f}^{′}(2) & \\frac{1}{2!}{f}^{″}(2) \\\\ 0 & f(2) & {f}^{′}(2) \\\\ 0 & 0 & f(2)\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{ln}⁡2 & \\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{1}{2}(-\\frac{1}{4}) \\\\ 0 & \\operatorname{ln}⁡2 & \\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 0 & 0 & \\operatorname{ln}⁡2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{ln}⁡2 & \\frac{1}{2} & -\\frac{1}{8} \\\\ 0 & \\operatorname{ln}⁡2 & \\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 0 & 0 & \\operatorname{ln}⁡2\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186562471 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157271 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "706303c1-0e4c-55f7-8b62-5094938f85bc" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Value of a Function of a Jordan Decomposition"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "613b1292-599e-5175-a4de-dac872a76495" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561817} {:answer/id #uuid "650f951f-a1c7-5370-9079-613e1ed08f22" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561832} {:answer/id #uuid "69eb12dd-2688-5a53-91ae-fe2035e9de63" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561847} {:answer/id #uuid "70bc40d1-370d-5f28-96fb-58c2c278fc37" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561863} {:answer/id #uuid "d2c5f2de-8e97-5e34-b223-ff08b5bc179e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562112}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "650f951f-a1c7-5370-9079-613e1ed08f22" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561832} :answer-field/id #uuid "85a7cfaa-2021-5878-b715-b12be6d3a7f4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562308}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a906d22b-042f-5736-a4c7-747a5da98697" :question/math-academy-id "q-253490" :question/problem "Consider the following matrices:\n\n$$\nE=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\pi }{6} & 0 \\\\ \\frac{5\\pi }{6} & \\pi \\end{aligned}],\\,D=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\pi }{6} & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\pi \\end{aligned}],\\,P=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nGiven that $E=PD{P}^{-1},$ find $4\\operatorname{sin}⁡E.$" :question/worked-solution "Given a function $f$ and matrices $A$ and $S,$ where $S$ is invertible, we have\n\n$$\nf(SA{S}^{-1})=S\\cdot f(A)\\cdot {S}^{-1}.\n$$\n\nFor $f(x)=4\\operatorname{sin}⁡E$ and the given matrix $C,$ we have\n\n$$\n4\\operatorname{sin}⁡E=4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(PD{P}^{-1})=P\\cdot (4\\operatorname{sin}⁡D)\\cdot {P}^{-1}.\n$$\n\nNow, since $D$ is a diagonal matrix, we get\n\n$$\n4\\operatorname{sin}⁡D=[\\begin{aligned}4\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\frac{\\pi }{6} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi \\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nAlso, the inverse of $P$ is\n\n$$\n{P}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{1\\cdot 1-(-1)\\cdot 0}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4\\operatorname{sin}⁡E & =P\\cdot (4\\operatorname{sin}⁡D)\\cdot {P}^{-1} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186562436 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157270 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "87883002-67eb-5111-b15a-c5941bb33f9b" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Value of a Function of a Jordan Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ea0401e5-9d3a-57a5-b046-48a14ed96f7c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562164}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ea0401e5-9d3a-57a5-b046-48a14ed96f7c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562164} :answer-field/id #uuid "250a0410-56cf-50a6-9de1-7caaa7d5a608" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562244} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "aa32fab1-7f40-54da-a1e0-f1997cc223c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\ln(2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562007}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "aa32fab1-7f40-54da-a1e0-f1997cc223c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\ln(2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562007} :answer-field/id #uuid "8a725e18-61fa-5fa6-82d0-ff96754212ab" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562313} 